  "id": "intrusion-set--eb03e27c-f174-547e-856f-46a80cb406b6",
  "name": "GTG-20006",
  "description": "Automated operations end-to-end via AI-driven workflows — development, infrastructure acquisition, phishing, persistence, C2, and exfiltration. Notably, monitoring AI agents that detected their own malware being flagged by a security product would autonomously modify and rebuild it to evade the new detection. Deployed custom Windows implants, a mobile exploitation kit, a browser-credential stealer, and a phishing platform mimicking government organizations; used device-code phishing, DNS hijacking of hospitality vendors, and WhatsApp account takeovers against Ukrainian/European government, military, diplomatic, and defense targets. Anthropic",
  "category": "A",
